PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Public Services Committee was held on Tuesday, December 3, 2024. in
Committee Room 104 and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were
as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Scott Roybal. Chairnian: Pete Laybourn; Dr. Mark Rinne; and Tom
Segrave.
AGENDA ITEMS
6.
ORDINANCE
READING
— Annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, tracts of
land situate in portions of Sections 4 and 5, TI3N, R67W, 6th P.M., Laramie County,
Wyoming (also known as ‘North Range Business Park’, located northwest of the 1-80 and
Roundtop Road interchange).
Mr. Segrave moved to approve on 3rd and final reading, seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion carned by
unanimous voice votc.
Seth Lloyd, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report.
7.
ORDINANCE —3 READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne establishing the zoning classification of LI Light Industrial and BP Business
Park for tracts of land being annexed to the City situate in portions of Sections 4 and 5.
TI 3N, R67W, 6th P.M., Laramie County, Wyoming (also known as ‘North Range Business
Park’. located northwcst of the 1-80 and Roundtop Road interchange).
Dr. Rinne moved to approve on 3 and final reading, seconded by Mr. Segravc. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Seth Lloyd, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and Dante Rushton,
LEADS Director of Real Estate & Property Management, thanked the committee and staff for the
recent approval of the business park zoning district.
8.
ORDINANCE —3 READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne changing the zoning classificalion from AG Agricultural and III heavy
Industrial to AG Agricultural for land located south of Campstool Rd and north of Interstate
80
I’.r. Segrave moved to approve on 3rd and final reading. seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Brandon Gilchrist. Planning & Development Department. provided a staff report.
