25.
RESOLUTION
Encouraging City staff to solicit public comment on changes to the
administration of sanitation pickup locations and further directing City staff to coordinate
with Univerus, Inc. to schedule a meeting before the Govenung Body regarding the
Sanitation Rerouting and Optimization Project. (SPONSOR
— MR. LAYBOURN)
Mr. Laybourn moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Segrave. Motion failed with Dr. Rinne and Mr.
Segrave voting “NO” and Mr. Layboum voting “YES.”
Pete Laybourn, Ward I Councilman and sponsor of the item, provided an overview of the proposed
resolution and thanked Vieki Nemecek. Public Works Director, for meeting with him to discuss
the proposed resolution.
Ms. Nemeeek also provided information related to proposed resolution
and advised a council work session has been scheduled for January 17. 2025. to discuss the
optimization of sanitation routes as recommended by Univerus. Craig LaVoy, Public Works
